From 144028c2e75215278151b6de77a875acd9200ca6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:03:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] English edition on the web: /en routes, language switch,
 English dashboard fields

The API, translator and hourly job already serve English (?lang=en); this
adds the website side.

- Reader pages under /en (home, story, section, search, 404) with English
  text from lib/i18n.ts; the language comes from the URL.
- Header link to the same page in the other language; <html lang> follows.
- Public services pass ?lang=en only on the English site, so Nepali
  requests stay as they were.
- An untranslated story on the English site shows the Nepali with a note.
- English dates, digits, weather city names, ads label and photo credits.
- Article editor: English title/summary/story, translation status and
  "translate now"; English is sent only when a person changed it, so
  machine translations keep updating.
- Categories: English name field. Article list: EN badge.
- CLAUDE.md: English edition section.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xort4sGQiveBkXPKQVyxNV
